# The PATHWAY - BONANZA's map between courses (wave 8R, SPEC.md 137.22).  The SHIPPED map: option A of
# docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/ (the owner's concept sketch, "Faithful"), page 0 as the owner marked it
# up (2026-11-19), and since 2026-11-25 THREE pages carrying the owner's ORDER of that day (SPEC.md 137.22.11;
# docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/README.md, "The journey"): "kite where mill is currently, with mill moving
# after it on the path, and loadstone where moon currently is, with caste after it, and keep after that
# splitting into two; with the treasury allowing a course skip".  THE ORDER IS DECIDED ONLY UP TO DOWNHILL
# DECISION, and pages 1 and 2 are NOT designed ("what is there was just prototype"): everything past page 0
# here is a working layout, each choice one line.  The marble AUTO-ROLLS along a route between glowing pads:
# finishing course A by exit E opens the one route keyed (A, E), whose gate sinks; an arrow on that route's
# side of the screen takes it, Enter plays the pad's course.
#
#   page 2 (top):     BOUNCE TRIAL'                         SUMMIT RUSH' (up a ramp)
#                       ^ up                                   ^
#                     PLAYGROUND' <-up-left- MOONLIT GREEN'    |
#                       ^ SECRET (the treasury)   ^ up         | up the right-hand climb
#   page 1 (middle):    +---<-up-left---- CLOCKWORK KEEP     WINDMILL LANE
#                                           ^ up               ^
#                                         CASTLE CLIMB         | up the right-hand climb
#                                           ^ up               |
#   page 0 (bottom):                      LODESTONE GORGE    KITE HILL
#                                           ^ up-left (exit 1)  ^ up (exit 0)
#                                           +--- DOWNHILL DECISION
#                                                  ^ up the right-hand road
#                      FIRST ROLL -right-> LITTLE HOP
#
# The REAL courses: FIRST ROLL (ROLL), LITTLE HOP (HOP), DOWNHILL DECISION (DOWN: its two exits the split); by
# its exit 0 KITE HILL (KITE) then WINDMILL LANE (MILL); by its exit 1 LODESTONE GORGE (LODE), CASTLE CLIMB
# (CASTL) and CLOCKWORK KEEP (KEEP), whose two exits split again.  The four old test courses (marked ' above)
# still stand in on pads of their own, so every course of the default build has a pad (the TEST courses,
# BZ_TESTCRS, SPEC.md 137.54, have none: the owner, 2026-11-19): SUMMIT RUSH (PEAK) ends the right-hand branch
# after WINDMILL LANE as it did; MOONLIT GREEN (MOON), PLAYGROUND (PLAY) and the OLD First Roll (FIRST, labelled
# "Bounce Trial" so no two pads read FIRST ROLL) follow CLOCKWORK KEEP's exit 0 (the throne) in the order they
# had.  CLOCKWORK KEEP's HIDDEN exit 1 (the treasury) is the map's one SECRET route, a SHORTCUT: straight to
# PLAYGROUND, SKIPPING MOONLIT GREEN.
#
# PAD NUMBERS: pads 0 - 7 play the courses they played (MILL is still pad 3, PEAK 4, MOON 5, PLAY 6, FIRST 7),
# on other cells past pad 2; the new courses are pads 8 (KITE), 9 (LODE), 10 (KEEP) and 11 (CASTL).  A route's
# number is its line's place below (the save's opened and taken bits, SPEC.md 137.22.5).  Every cell is 13
# further along both axes than before 2026-11-25 (208 lines down the picture: room for page 2 above), which
# moves nothing on page 0.
#
# The icons are docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/gen.py's (32 x 24; placeholders for the stand-ins), and so
# is the scenery, three `art` pieces (gen.py --ship).  A screen direction is a ground step: +x down-right, -x
# up-left, +y down-left, -y up-right; both axes at once (equal amounts) down, up, left or right.
course PATH "The Pathway"
width  64
ball   rubber
pathway
version 2                                   # the SAVE's (SPEC.md 137.22.5.1): 2 since 2026-11-25 - the pads past
                                            # DOWNHILL DECISION play other courses and the routes are other routes,
                                            # so a game saved on the old map is emptied (its best times are kept:
                                            # they go by course)
music  fairway                              # (8b.10 gives the pathway its own)
rail   crystal                              # the route material (SPEC.md 137.22.8)
view   0 540                                # page 0's CGA window: 8 lines up, so the gate on Lodestone Gorge's
                                            # road on and the titles there are wholly on page 0 (the owner's
                                            # mark-up; 332 + 208)
pages  3
titles 5x7                                  # the map's titles in the 5 x 7 face (SPEC.md 137.22.2, 2026-11-19)
float  rect 0 0 64 64                       # the whole map FLOATS (the owner, 2026-11-16): crystal islands
                                            # with short icicle faces are the pathway's look (SPEC.md 137.27.2)

# pad N COURSE WX WY
pad 0 ROLL  34 41                           # First Roll: where a new game rests
pad 1 HOP   37 38                           # Little Hop
pad 2 DOWN  37 30                           # Downhill Decision: two exits, the split
pad 3 MILL  25 18                           # Windmill Lane (page 1): after Kite Hill
pad 4 PEAK  15 10                           # (page 2, 2 units up) Summit Rush standing in: the right-hand branch's end
pad 5 MOON  11 13
                                            # treasury SKIPS
pad 6 PLAY   6 13
pad 7 FIRST  3 10
                                            # (the map has the real First Roll on pad 0): the left-hand branch's end
pad 8 KITE  33 26                           # Kite Hill, where Windmill Lane was
pad 9 LODE  28 30                           # Lodestone Gorge, where Moonlit Green was
pad 10 KEEP 17 19
pad 11 CASTL 22 24                          # Castle Climb (page 1), where Playground was: before its castle

# route A B exit E [secret] [gate WX WY] path WX,WY[,H] ...
route 0 1 exit 0  path 34,41 37,38                  # First Roll -> Little Hop, right along the bottom road
route 1 2 exit 0  path 37,38 41,34 37,30            # Little Hop -> Downhill Decision, right then up
route 2 8 exit 0  path 37,30 33,26                  # Downhill Decision's exit 0 -> Kite Hill, UP (the Up arrow)
route 2 9 exit 1  path 37,30 28,30                  # Downhill Decision's exit 1 -> Lodestone Gorge, UP-LEFT (Left)
route 8 3 exit 0  path 33,26 25,18                  # Kite Hill -> Windmill Lane, up the right-hand climb into page 1
route 9 11 exit 0  gate 27 29  path 28,30 22,24     # Lodestone Gorge -> Castle Climb, up into page 1
route 11 10 exit 0  path 22,24 17,19
route 10 5 exit 0  path 17,19 11,13
                                                    # page 2
route 5 6 exit 0  path 11,13 6,13
route 6 7 exit 0  path 6,13 3,10
route 3 4 exit 0  path 25,18 17,10 15,10,2          # Windmill Lane -> Summit Rush: up into page 2, then up-left UP A
                                                    # RAMP to the summit (2 units in one cell)
route 10 6 exit 1 secret  path 17,19 12,19 6,13
                                                    # Moonlit Green: a SHORTCUT, drawn only once it is taken

# icon N FILE SX SY [fps F] [title "TEXT"] [tdx DX]: frame 0 the rest pose, the rest while the marble rests
# here; a title on the map in place of the course's ("|" breaks a line), DX px off the icon's centre
icon 0 icons/first32x24.bba       -128 576
icon 1 icons/frog32x24.bba         -32 576
icon 2 icons/fork32x24.bba          56 560  title "Downhill|Decision"  tdx -25
icon 3 icons/mill32x24.bba          56 360  tdx -21
icon 4 icons/summit32x24.bba        64 152
icon 5 icons/moon32x24.bba           8 176  tdx -8
icon 6 icons/playground32x24.bba   -72 136  tdx 8
icon 7 icons/trial32x24.bba        -72  88  title "Bounce Trial"  tdx 14
icon 8 icons/kite32x24.bba          56 464
icon 9 icons/lode32x24.bba         -80 464  title "Lodestone|Gorge"  tdx -26
icon 10 icons/keep32x24.bba          8 272  title "Clockwork|Keep"  tdx 8
icon 11 icons/castl32x24.bba      -104 352

# the SCENERY: art FILE SX SY (SPEC.md 137.23.2), px from page 0's CGA window's top-left corner, painted over
# the finished picture - so each piece stands in open sky, clear of every route, icon and title.  gen.py --ship
# writes the three files.  None is KEEP's: its pad is the one most likely to move.
art path_kites.bba  200 -48                 # Kite Hill's kites, their strings down behind its title to its icon
art path_cragw.bba   40 -64                 # the gorge's west wall: the mine's adit and an ore cart
art path_crage.bba  168 -48                 # the gorge's east wall: a vein of lodestone

# the lives, one counter a page
lives 29 36
lives 21 17
lives  7  5
